* The first argument specifies the input JSON file(s) to process. This can either be a single file or multiple files separated by spaces. If multiple files are specified, they will be processed in parallel using separate threads.
* The second argument specifies the fields that should be included in the final output. These fields can be any valid JSON path expression, such as "name" for a top-level field or "address.city" for a nested field. Multiple fields can be specified by separating them with spaces. If no fields are specified, all records will be returned.
