To integrate with an external API, this implementation uses an asynchronous function to make HTTP GET requests for each element's metadata. It also respects rate limits and handles potential network failures gracefully using try-catch blocks. The `traverseDOM` function returns a promise that resolves once all matching elements have been traversed and their metadata has been fetched or cached."]

