    HttpClient client = new HttpClient(config);

    // Send an HTTP request to retrieve data from a remote server
    String response = client.get("https://api.example.com/data");

    // Parse the JSON response using the JSONDeserializer
    Object parsedResponse = new JSONDeserializer().deserialize(response, null);

    // ...
}
```
In this example, we are creating a new `HttpClient` instance with the configured settings for the "my-app" application. We then use this client to send an HTTP request to retrieve data from a remote server and parse the response using the `JSONDeserializer`. The resulting parsed object can be used in the rest of our code as needed.

This example demonstrates how to use the `ExternalConfig` module to interact with an external configuration management system, allowing us to simplify the process of managing and deploying applications across multiple environments while reducing the risk of leaking sensitive data.']

