class StreamAndTransformData extends EventEmitter {
  constructor() {
    super();
    this.dataSources = new Map();
    this.dataFormats = new Map([
      ['json', JSONStream],
      ['xml', XMLStream],
      ['csv', CSVStream],
      ['binary', BinaryProtocolStream]
    ]);
    this.backpressureStrategies = new Map([
      ['none', () => {}],
      ['throttling', this.throttleBackpressureStrategy],
      ['buffering', this.bufferBackpressureStrategy]
    ]);
  }

  addDataSource(dataSource) {
    if (!this.dataSources.has(dataSource)) {
      this.dataSources.set(dataSource, new Set());
    }
  }

  removeDataSource(dataSource) {
    if (this.dataSources.has(dataSource)) {
      this.dataSources.delete(dataSource);
    }
  }

  addDataFormat(format, transformFunction) {
    if (!this.dataFormats.has(format)) {
      this.dataFormats.set(format, transformFunction);
    }
  }

  removeDataFormat(format) {
    if (this.dataFormats.has(format)) {
      this.dataFormats.delete(format);
    }
  }

  addBackpressureStrategy(strategy, backpressureFunction) {
    if (!this.backpressureStrategies.has(strategy)) {
      this.backpressureStrategies.set(strategy, backpressureFunction);
    }
  }

  removeBackpressureStrategy(strategy) {
    if (this.backpressureStrategies.has(strategy)) {
      this.backpressureStrategies.delete(strategy);
    }
  }

  async start() {
    for (const [dataSource, transformFunctions] of this.dataSources) {
      const dataFormat = this.getDataFormat(dataSource.type);
      if (dataFormat) {
        const stream = await dataSource.connect();
        const backpressureStrategy = this.getBackpressureStrategy(dataSource.backpressure);
        const transformStream = new Transform({
          objectMode: true,
          transform: async (chunk, encoding, callback) => {
            try {
              const transformedData = await dataFormat.transform(chunk);
              backpressureStrategy(transformedData);
              this.emit('data', transformedData);
              callback();
            } catch (error) {
              console.log(`Error transforming data: ${error}`);
              callback(error);
            }
          }
        });
        stream.pipe(transformStream);
      }
    }
  }

  stop() {
    for (const [dataSource, transformFunctions] of this.dataSources) {
      dataSource.disconnect();
    }
  }

  getDataFormat(type) {
    return this.dataFormats.get(type);
  }

  getBackpressureStrategy(backpressure) {
    return this.backpressureStrategies.get(backpressure);
  }
}
```
This library is designed to handle multiple data sources, each with its own unique data format and backpressure strategy. It provides a way to add or remove data sources, as well as customize the data formats and backpressure strategies used for each source. The library also includes support for asynchronous message queueing using `messageQueue`, which allows for low-latency data delivery and fault-tolerant operations.

The `StreamAndTransformData` class extends the `EventEmitter` class, allowing it to emit events when data is transformed and ready to be consumed by other parts of the application or external systems. It also includes support for efficient buffering and flow control mechanisms, as well as customizable backpressure strategies based on resource constraints and application requirements.

The library provides a `start` method that initializes all data sources and sets up the necessary pipelines to handle streaming data. The `stop` method is used to shut down the library and release any resources that may be in use.

In order to add or remove data sources, the `addDataSource` and `removeDataSource` methods can be used. These methods take a single argument, which is an object with information about the data source, such as its type and connection details. The `addDataFormat` and `removeDataFormat` methods are used to customize the data formats used for each data source, while the `addBackpressureStrategy` and `removeBackpressureStrategy` methods allow for customizing the backpressure strategies used for each data source.

The library includes support for multiple output formats for transformed data, allowing for flexible consumption by different parts of the application or external systems. This is done through the use of a `TransformStream`, which allows for customization of the data format and transformation rules. The `addOutputFormat` method can be used to add a new output format, while the `removeOutputFormat` method can be used to remove an existing output format.

The library is designed to be modular, allowing for easy addition of new data formats, transformation rules, and output destinations. This is achieved through the use of a `Map` data structure for storing data sources, data formats, and backpressure strategies. The `addDataSource`, `removeDataSource`, `addDataFormat`, `removeDataFormat`, `addBackpressureStrategy`, and `removeBackpressureStrategy` methods can be used to add or remove individual components of the library.

The library also includes comprehensive documentation and unit tests, making it easier for developers to integrate and maintain. The `start` method returns a promise that resolves only after all data has been successfully processed and transformed, ensuring a seamless user experience."]

