The system provides a flexible command-line interface for specifying batch processing parameters, including concurrency limits, query timeouts, and custom transformation rules, allowing administrators to fine-tune performance based on system load and resource availability. It enables administrators to specify processing priorities for files based on business-criticality and defines custom rules for file classification.

The system optimizes the system for both time and space complexity, balancing speed, accuracy, and resource usage in scenarios involving millions of files. It utilizes memory-mapped files and asynchronous I/O operations to minimize system calls and maximize throughput. It implements data compression techniques for infrequently accessed files to reduce storage footprint without impacting performance.

The system ensures the system can scale horizontally by incorporating load balancing and sharding strategies to distribute processing tasks across multiple nodes, accommodating increases in file volume and metadata repository load without significant performance degradation. It uses containerization to simplify deployment and scaling across different cloud providers.

