To ensure scalability, the microservice uses dynamic load balancing across multiple endpoints to optimize performance based on current system load and geographical proximity of clients. It also includes robust error handling and retry mechanisms to handle transient failures and consistent operation during failures.

The microservice is designed with security best practices in mind, including data privacy and protection against potential threats. It collaborates with stakeholders to define service-level agreements (SLAs) and ensures the service meets business objectives and user expectations."]

