Here's a sample code block that can be used to implement a modular, scalable PHP service for diverse user authentication needs:
```php
<?php

namespace App\Services;

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Cache;
use GuzzleHttp\Client as HttpClient;
use Psr\Http\Message\ResponseInterface;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Request;
use Symfony\Component\Security\Core\Authentication\Token\UsernamePasswordToken;
use Symfony\Component\Security\Core\User\UserProviderInterface;
use Symfony\Component\Security\Core\Exception\AuthenticationException;

class AuthenticationService implements UserProviderInterface
{
    protected $httpClient;
    protected $userProvider;
    protected $tokenStorage;
    protected $cache;

    public function __construct(HttpClient $httpClient, UserProviderInterface $userProvider)
    {
        $this->httpClient = $httpClient;
        $this->userProvider = $userProvider;
        $this->tokenStorage = new TokenStorage();
        $this->cache = Cache::store('redis');
    }

    public function authenticate(Request $request): ?UserInterface
    {
        // Get the access token from the request headers or query parameters
        $accessToken = $request->headers->get('Authorization') ?? $request->query->get('access_token');

        // Check if the access token is valid and retrieve the user information
        try {
            $response = $this->httpClient->get($this->userProvider->getUserInformationEndpoint(), [
                'headers' => [
                    'Authorization' => 'Bearer ' . $accessToken,
                ],
            ]);

            $userInfo = json_decode($response->getBody()->getContents(), true);
        } catch (AuthenticationException $e) {
            // Token is invalid or expired. Refresh the token if possible.
            try {
                $refreshToken = $this->tokenStorage->getRefreshToken($accessToken);
                $response = $this->httpClient->post($this->userProvider->getUserInformationEndpoint(), [
                    'headers' => [
                        'Authorization' => 'Bearer ' . $refreshToken,
                    ],
                ]);

                $userInfo = json_decode($response->getBody()->getContents(), true);
                $this->tokenStorage->storeUserInformation($userInfo);
            } catch (AuthenticationException $e) {
                // Token is still invalid. Redirect the user to the login page with an error message.
                return null;
            }
        }

        // Store the access token and refresh token in cache for later use
        $this->cache->set('access_token', $accessToken);
        $this->cache->set('refresh_token', $refreshToken ?? '');

        // Create a Symfony UserInterface object from the user information and return it
        return new User($userInfo['username'], $userInfo['password']);
    }

    public function refreshTokens(Request $request): void
    {
        // Get the access token from cache or the request headers or query parameters
        $accessToken = $this->cache->get('access_token') ?? $request->headers->get('Authorization') ?? $request->query->get('access_token');

        if (!$accessToken) {
            return;
        }

        // Check if the access token is valid and retrieve the user information
        try {
            $response = $this->httpClient->get($this->userProvider->getUserInformationEndpoint(), [
                'headers' => [
                    'Authorization' => 'Bearer ' . $accessToken,
                ],
            ]);

            $userInfo = json_decode($response->getBody()->getContents(), true);
        } catch (AuthenticationException $e) {
            // Token is invalid or expired. Refresh the token if possible.
            try {
                $refreshToken = $this->tokenStorage->getRefreshToken($accessToken);
                $response = $this->httpClient->post($this->userProvider->getUserInformationEndpoint(), [
                    'headers' => [
                        'Authorization' => 'Bearer ' . $refreshToken,
                    ],
                ]);

                $userInfo = json_decode($response->getBody()->getContents(), true);
                $this->tokenStorage->storeUserInformation($userInfo);
            } catch (AuthenticationException $e) {
                // Token is still invalid. Redirect the user to the login page with an error message.
                return;
            }
        }

        // Store the access token and refresh token in cache for later use
        $this->cache->set('access_token', $accessToken);
        $this->cache->set('refresh_token', $refreshToken ?? '');
    }
}
```
This code block implements the `UserProviderInterface` from Symfony to handle user authentication and retrieval of user information. It uses a Guzzle HTTP client to make requests to an OAuth 2.0 provider for token validation, and it stores the access tokens in cache to reduce the number of requests made to the provider during high traffic.

The `authenticate` method is called whenever a request is made to a protected route, and it checks if the access token is valid by making a GET request to the user information endpoint with the `Authorization` header set to `Bearer <access_token>`. If the token is invalid or expired, it refreshes the token by making a POST request to the same endpoint with the `Authorization` header set to `Bearer <refresh_token>`, and it stores the new access token in cache.

The `refreshTokens` method is called periodically to ensure that tokens are still valid and not expired. It retrieves the access token from cache or the request headers or query parameters, checks if the token is valid by making a GET request to the user information endpoint with the `Authorization` header set to `Bearer <access_token>`, and stores the new access token in cache if it is still valid.

