5. Optimize performance by minimizing latency during heavy loads by using asynchronous I/O for external data retrieval concurrently with other tasks. Monitor and adjust resource usage dynamically based on system load and available memory.
6. Ensure thread safety and maintain data integrity by handling concurrent access, employing atomic operations and lock-free data structures where appropriate. Implement efficient memory management to prevent fragmentation.
7. Support dynamic growth of the list of `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures, adding new entries while preventing exceedance of a predefined maximum size. Implement scalable memory allocation strategies to accommodate for this.']

