}
```
9. Code Maintainability and Testing: The code should be designed to ensure robustness and ease of maintenance, with a focus on reducing the complexity and increasing readability. This can be achieved by using a consistent coding style, naming conventions, and test cases that cover all critical paths.
```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <assert.h>
#include <unistd.h> // For sleep()

