The `ConfigurationManager` class is responsible for fetching the latest version of the configuration from the RESTful API and caching it in memory. The `GetConfigurationAsync` method returns the cached version of the configuration if available, or makes a request to the API and caches the result before returning it.

### Configuration File

The `appsettings.json` file contains the settings for the application. In this example, we'll use it to store the URL of the RESTful API that provides the configuration.

```json
{
  "Url": "https://api.example.com/v1"
}
```

### Startup Class

The `Startup` class is used to configure the application and its dependencies. In this example, we'll add a dependency on the `ConfigurationManager` class and use it to fetch the configuration from the API and cache it in memory.

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Builder;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Hosting;
using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
using WebApplication1.ConfigurationManagement;

namespace WebApplication1
{
    public class Startup
    {
        public void ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection services)
        {
            // Add the ConfigurationManager as a service
            services.AddSingleton<IConfigurationManager, ConfigurationManager>();
        }

        public void Configure(IApplicationBuilder app, IHostingEnvironment env)
        {
            // Use the ConfigurationManager to fetch the configuration and cache it in memory
            var configManager = app.ApplicationServices.GetService<IConfigurationManager>();
            configManager.GetConfigurationAsync("ConfigName").Wait();
        }
    }
}
```

### Controller Class

The `Controller` class is used to handle HTTP requests and responses. In this example, we'll add a method that uses the cached configuration to retrieve a value from the RESTful API.

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
using WebApplication1.ConfigurationManagement;

namespace WebApplication1.Controllers
{
    public class ValuesController : Controller
    {
        private readonly IConfigurationManager _configManager;

        public ValuesController(IConfigurationManager configManager)
        {
            _configManager = configManager;
        }

        [HttpGet]
        public async Task<string> GetValue()
        {
            // Use the cached configuration to retrieve a value from the RESTful API
            var config = await _configManager.GetConfigurationAsync("ConfigName");
            return config["Key"];
        }
    }
}
```

In this example, we use the `IConfigurationManager` interface to fetch the cached configuration and retrieve a value from the RESTful API. The `GetValue` method returns the retrieved value as a string.

### Testing the Application

To test the application, navigate to the URL for the `ValuesController` in your web browser. You should see the value that was retrieved from the RESTful API.

If you make changes to the configuration on the RESTful API and re-run the application, it will automatically pick up the new configuration and display the updated value.']

