We also optimize for low-latency session lookups and updates by implementing advanced caching strategies such as cache invalidation policies, bloom filters for key existence checks, and time-to-live (TTL) settings to minimize the risk of stale data and ensure data integrity under high concurrency.

We design the system to scale horizontally, handling uneven load patterns and potential hotspots. We implement failover strategies to maintain session availability during network partitions, ensuring minimal impact on user experience. We introduce a session sharding mechanism based on user geolocation and role to improve performance.

