The class is designed for flexibility and customization by allowing game developers to specify probability distributions for generating random values, with flexibility for tuning randomness characteristics to balance predictability and variability. The class also includes error handling mechanisms to manage invalid range inputs, network errors, and unexpected data formats, providing detailed logging and monitoring capabilities.

The class is designed to be backward compatible for future enhancements by using version control and code reviews to manage changes effectively. The class includes comprehensive unit tests covering all aspects of the implementation, ensuring robustness and reliability. The class also includes end-to-end tests that simulate real-world usage scenarios, further testing the stability and performance of the class under various conditions.

