The code uses a cache pool class that manages multiple caches with different backend types and eviction policies, allowing developers to create caches with different properties based on their needs. The cache wrapper class provides methods for accessing the cache pool, while the cache client class provides methods for accessing the cache wrapper.

This implementation includes support for auto-scaling in response to varying loads using container orchestration tools like Kubernetes, while maintaining thread safety and low-latency access under high concurrency. The system also prioritizes user experience and interface design by providing an intuitive API that provides detailed performance statistics for each operation.

Overall, this code block demonstrates a robust and scalable distributed cache system using C++, with a focus on performance, reliability, and usability.']

