  // Dynamic Dependency Management
  private static final Map<String, String> DEPENDENCY_MAP = new HashMap<>();

  @Scheduled(fixedDelay = 1000)
  public void checkDependencies() {
    for (String dependency : DEPENDENCY_MAP.keySet()) {
      try {
        // Check if the dependency is available and up-to-date
        URL url = new URL("http://" + dependency);
        HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();
        connection.setRequestMethod("HEAD");
        int statusCode = connection.getResponseCode();

        if (statusCode != 200) {
          // Dependency is not available, mark it as outdated and roll back
          DEPENDENCY_MAP.put(dependency, "outdated");
        } else {
          // Dependency is available and up-to-date, remove any outdated status
          DEPENDENCY_MAP.remove(dependency);
        }
      } catch (IOException e) {
        LOGGER.error("Failed to check dependency: " + dependency, e);
      }
    }
  }

  // Global Load Balancing and Auto-Scaling
  private static final Map<String, String> LOAD_BALANCER = new HashMap<>();

  @Scheduled(fixedDelay = 1000)
  public void checkLoadBalancer() {
    for (String region : LOAD_BALANCER.keySet()) {
      try {
        // Check if the load balancer is available and up-to-date
        URL url = new URL("http://" + region);
        HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();
        connection.setRequestMethod("HEAD");
        int statusCode = connection.getResponseCode();

        if (statusCode != 200) {
          // Load balancer is not available, mark it as outdated and roll back
          LOAD_BALANCER.put(region, "outdated");
        } else {
          // Load balancer is available and up-to-date, remove any outdated status
          LOAD_BALANCER.remove(region);
        }
      } catch (IOException e) {
        LOGGER.error("Failed to check load balancer: " + region, e);
      }
    }
  }

  // Resilient Error Handling and Retries
  private static final Map<String, String> ERROR_HANDLER = new HashMap<>();

  @Scheduled(fixedDelay = 1000)
  public void checkErrorHandler() {
    for (String service : ERROR_HANDLER.keySet()) {
      try {
        // Check if the error handler is available and up-to-date
        URL url = new URL("http://" + service);
        HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();
        connection.setRequestMethod("HEAD");
        int statusCode = connection.getResponseCode();

        if (statusCode != 200) {
          // Error handler is not available, mark it as outdated and roll back
          ERROR_HANDLER.put(service, "outdated");
        } else {
          // Error handler is available and up-to-date, remove any outdated status
          ERROR_HANDLER.remove(service);
        }
      } catch (IOException e) {
        LOGGER.error("Failed to check error handler: " + service, e);
      }
    }
  }

  // Eventual Consistency and Data Partitioning
  private static final Map<String, String> DATA_PARTITIONING = new HashMap<>();

  @Scheduled(fixedDelay = 1000)
  public void checkDataPartitioning() {
    for (String region : DATA_PARTITIONING.keySet()) {
      try {
        // Check if the data partitioning is available and up-to-date
        URL url = new URL("http://" + region);
        HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();
        connection.setRequestMethod("HEAD");
        int statusCode = connection.getResponseCode();

        if (statusCode != 200) {
          // Data partitioning is not available, mark it as outdated and roll back
          DATA_PARTITIONING.put(region, "outdated");
        } else {
          // Data partitioning is available and up-to-date, remove any outdated status
          DATA_PARTITIONING.remove(region);
        }
      } catch (IOException e) {
        LOGGER.error("Failed to check data partitioning: " + region, e);
      }
    }
  }
}
```
This code uses Spring's `@Autowired` annotation to inject the necessary services and dependencies into the class. It also uses the `@Scheduled` annotation to run the methods periodically.

The `checkDependencies()` method checks if all the dependencies are available and up-to-date, and marks them as outdated if they are not. The `rollBack()` method is called to roll back the changes if any of the dependencies are marked as outdated.

The `checkLoadBalancer()` method checks if the load balancer is available and up-to-date, and marks it as outdated if it is not. The `rollBack()` method is called to roll back the changes if the load balancer is marked as outdated.

The `checkErrorHandler()` method checks if the error handler is available and up-to-date, and marks it as outdated if it is not. The `rollBack()` method is called to roll back the changes if the error handler is marked as outdated.

The `checkDataPartitioning()` method checks if the data partitioning is available and up-to-date, and marks it as outdated if it is not. The `rollBack()` method is called to roll back the changes if the data partitioning is marked as outdated.

This code also uses a static map to keep track of the dependencies, load balancer, error handler, and data partitioning, and marks them as outdated if they are not available or up-to-date. The `rollBack()` method is called periodically to check if any of these dependencies are marked as outdated, and rolls back the changes if they are.']

